From b8b3d536eaa08748adc4970725d665119b6f7b9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:27:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): hub resume accepts a runner-only
 active_pr hold after any latest transition

Problem: `hermes kanban resume` on the hub (core 3f3789037c5) refused t_01a1d120e7d7c686 with
"resume requires an active_pr hold (guard: none)" while pool workers 1-6 logged
`Held cards: t_01a1d120e7d7c686=active_pr`. Operators fell back to `schedule --clock-only` + `unblock`
(again for t_01a1d09d3547337b, 2026-11-13 02:42Z).

Why 1: resume trusted only the hub's own check_respawn_guard, which returned None; the hold existed
  only in the runners' evaluation (their respawn_guarded events replicate to the hub: hub kanban.db
  rows 1160747, 1161849, 1164966).
Why 2: 7cc74b2d05 added observed(): a replicated respawn_guarded active_pr after the latest lifecycle
  transition counts - but only when that transition is one of promoted/promoted_manual/unblocked/
  reopened/reclaimed/created.
Why 3: a card becomes ready again through many other paths whose latest transition is not in that
  list: the same-profile reassign tried in this incident (`assigned` 21:50:29, runners re-held at
  21:50:32 = row 1164966), a woken continuation (`continued` + continuation_woken), a woken park
  (`scheduled` + condition_met), a released claim (`claimed` + released), changes_requested, a
  triage sweep after `blocked`, and a resume the runners did not honour (`operator_resumed`).
  After any of them resume refused although the runners held the card.
Root (happened): the episode rule tried to name "ready transitions" instead of asking whether the
  observation itself (a dispatcher writes respawn_guarded only for a card in its ready/review lane,
  and re-writes it after every other event: guard_hold_reason) follows the latest transition.
Root (not caught): tests built only promoted -> respawn_guarded; no test replayed real Board
  histories or the reassign workaround shape.
Recurrence: second fix on this path (7cc74b2d05 covered the promoted shape only).

Fix: the episode starts at the latest transition of any kind; an active_pr observation after it
proves a current hold. Observations before any later transition still don't count, the local
guard's other reasons still win, the Board-replica read stays bound to the home boundary UID, and
resume() still requires an unclaimed READY card on its home gateway (review cards refused there).

Proof:
- New tests fail on origin/main c559287b51 with "guard: none" (7 parametrized observed cases + the
  real-gateway reassign test) and pass after; 120 tests across operator_resume*, observed_pr_hold
  boundaries and review_release* pass.
- test_home_resume_accepts_a_worker_hold_recorded_after_a_reassign: real hub + worker stores and
  Board feed; hub same-profile reassign, worker re-holds, hub guard None, hub resume, worker claims.
- Boundary test "parked" now parks AFTER the hold (old version asserted a hold seen after a park is
  stale, which the replay contradicts); new test covers a hold seen after each kind.
- Replay (Board replica default/hermes/bb/askeve + worker-1 kanban.db, mode=ro): every active_pr
  respawn_guarded event classified by its latest transition. Newly accepted points: continued 6216
  events/26 cards, changes_requested 2053/1, assigned 757/7 (incl. t_01a1d120e7d7c686), scheduled
  133/11, claimed(+released) 92/21, operator_resumed 10/1, dependency_wait 2/1, blocked(+triage
  sweep) 2/2. Samples read: each was a ready card still held, except dependency_wait (a runner copy
  that had not yet seen the demotion; card was todo, so resume's READY check refuses it). Current
  card states: 0 cards change verdict today.
